      "Saint Chrysanthus and Saint Daria": 1,
      "Chrysanthus and Daria were Roman martyrs buried on the Via Salaria Nova. Their tombs were publicly honored and their names appear in an early martyrology, so they were already venerated in Rome in the fourth century. A later legend says Chrysanthus was the son of a noble family of Alexandria who became a Christian in Rome, and that Daria, a Vestal, was won to the faith through him; it says both were stoned to death in a sandpit on the Via Salaria. The Catholic Encyclopedia notes that the surviving Acts have no historical value, but the martyrdom and the veneration of their tombs are certain.": 1,
      "Read about Saints Chrysanthus and Daria": 1,
      "25.10.2026": 1,
      "C": 2,
      "25 Oct": 1,
      "Saint Demetrius of Thessalonica": 1,
      "Demetrius is remembered as a martyr and as the protector of the city of Thessalonica, in Greece. Catholic Online describes him as a deacon martyred at Sirmium and says early legends credit him with a military career. The Catholic Encyclopedia records that an oil said to work miracles flowed from his tomb. He was very popular in the Middle Ages.": 1,
      "Brief story based on Catholic Online and the Catholic Encyclopedia.": 1,
      "Read about Saint Demetrius": 1,
