      "Saint Terence and Companions": 1,
      "The Maronite calendar lists Terence and his companions on October 28. We have matched this entry to the group of martyrs Terence, Africanus, Pompeius and their companions, because the names fit; the calendar itself gives no details. According to Catholic Online, they were martyred in the persecution under Emperor Decius, and tradition says they were forced into a pit filled with serpents and stinging reptiles, and those who survived were beheaded. Catholic Online gives their feast as April 10, while the Orthodox Church in America lists Africanus, Terence, Maximus, Pompeius and others of Carthage on October 28.": 1,
      "Brief story based on Catholic Online. The date follows the Maronite calendar.": 1,
      "Read about Saint Terence and his companions": 1,
      "28.10.2026": 1,
